\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Father, whose will is life and good\cf0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 For all of mortal breath,
\par Bind strong the bond of brotherhood
\par of those who fight with death.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Empower the hands and hearts and wills
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 of friends in lands afar,
\par Who battle with the body's ills,
\par And wage the holy war.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.\cf0   Where'er they heal the maimed and blind,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 Let love of Christ attend:
\par Proclaim the good Physician's mind,
\par  And prove the Saviour friend.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. For still His love works wondrous charms,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  And, as in days of old,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 He takes the wounded to His arms,
\par And bears them to the fold.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  O Father, look from heaven and
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 bless,Where'er Thy servants be,
\par Their works of pure unselfishness,
\par Made consecrate to Thee!\f1 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

